well as at the supermarket  but if you look even further into other  sectors there's some more good news  particularly in the semiconductor chip  manufacturing we all remember those  supply chain woes many of which we are  still feeling as a result of shortages  in the tech sector  if you look specifically at high tech  manufacturing and those semiconductor  chips point nine percent increase in  that particular sector since the start  of the pandemic that's good news for a  lot of folks looking for jobs but we  also should note that this report did  not factor into the handful of headlines  that have come out in recent weeks in  the financial press about companies like  walmart amazon twitter that have said  that at minimum they are reassessing  their hiring outlook and there was a  recent conference board survey that was  just published a few weeks ago a  mid-year outlook by top c-suite  executives and 60 percent of them jeff  feel that the economy is still headed  toward a recession  we will wait and see kevin surely thank  you for your insight  thank you
 

